Dissolved metal concentrations in all leachate samples were measured by inductively coupled plasma optical emission spectrometry (ICP-OES; Agilent 5800, Santa Clara, USA). Samples were diluted in 2 vol.% HNO 3  (TraceMetal grade, Fisher Scientific) before introduction to the instrument. External calibration used five-point curves constructed from certified multi-element standard solutions (Merck Certipur), achieving  R 2  ≥ 0.9999 for all target analytes. Yttrium at 1 mg L −1  was added as an internal standard to correct for matrix-induced suppression and any drift in instrument response over the analytical sequence. Replicate precision, expressed as relative standard deviation (RSD), remained below 3% across all measurements. Extraction efficiency for each metal M (EE m , %) was calculated from a straightforward mass balance: 2 EE m % = C leachate × V leachate / m solid × w m , feed × 100 , \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
